# Stream apply order for this project, most-dependent-first.
#
# ACROSS streams order normally does NOT matter -- streams touch disjoint files
# and commute (n64/CLAUDE.md). SuperMario64 is an exception: `cheats` and `book`
# BOTH touch src/game/mario.c. They do not collide today (the hunks sit ~370
# lines apart), but the book grows a doc-region per chapter and covers Mario's
# action machine, which is exactly what the cheats edit -- so the two will meet.
#
# `cheats` first, so the book's markers are placed against the cheated tree
# rather than the other way round: the cheats are the substantive code, the
# markers are commentary on whatever the code ends up being.
#
# `upstream-candidates` is not listed -- it only touches docs/building.md, so it
# is disjoint from both and applies afterwards, alphabetically.
#
# One stream per line; listed streams apply first, in this order. Comments and
# blank lines are ignored.
cheats
book
